# Authoritative ignore rules for the whole repository.
#
# A pattern containing a slash is anchored to the directory holding the
# .gitignore, so `backend/models/weights/*.pt` here would not match
# `app/backend/models/weights/`. Patterns below are therefore either bare names,
# which match at any depth, or prefixed with `**/`.

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# Model weights
# Shipped via a GitHub Release instead. best_cnn.pt is 90MB and best_hybrid.pt
# is 97MB, past GitHub's 50MB warning and near its 100MB hard limit.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.h5
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.npy

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
dissertation_env/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Datasets
# Named individually rather than ignoring `data/` wholesale: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, and data/metadata has to
# stay trackable. The `**/` negations keep the directory skeleton and its
# .gitkeep markers so a clone shows where the downloads belong.
**/data/raw/**
!**/data/raw/**/
!**/data/raw/**/.gitkeep
**/data/unseen/**
!**/data/unseen/**/
!**/data/unseen/**/.gitkeep
# MNW is a git clone, so the directory negation above would otherwise stage it
# as a gitlink pointing at a commit nothing in this repository can resolve.
# Listed after the negations because the last matching pattern wins.
**/data/unseen/MNW
# generated by split_dataset.py, so a clone does not need the skeleton
**/data/processed/
**/data/frequency_domain/
datasets/

# Training artefacts
# results/ is deliberately absent: it holds the metrics and figures behind every
# number in the dissertation and is tracked.
checkpoints/
logs/
runs/
outputs/
*.log

# Working notes, kept out of the repository
# AI usage is disclosed as a paragraph in the report rather than through these.
CLAUDE.md
testLog.md
completion_checklist.md
structure.md
.claude/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
